# GenSeo — operating rules for Cursor agents

This repo writes to the LIVE Shopify store wellnessnest.co. `AGENTS.md` (6 hard rules) is the authority and
`DAILY-RUN.md` is the daily runbook; this file is the Cursor summary plus the brand locks and the cloud-agent
boundary. Skills: `.cursor/skills/genseo-*` are pointers — always read the canonical `skills/genseo-*/SKILL.md`
in full before acting on one.

## Paths
`/Users/kevinkreative/genseo` and `~/genseo` in scripts, skills and tickets mean this repo root (`/workspace` on a
Cursor Cloud VM). Several scripts hard-code the Mac path (`genseo_roster.py`, `topic_fitness.py` caches,
`refresh_article_cache.py`), so on a cloud VM they read nothing or fail — that is expected, not a bug to patch.

## Cloud-agent boundary (default; only an explicit request from Kevin widens it)
- **Allowed:** article drafts, ticket and ideas-board edits, read-only checks against the public storefront
  (`/products.json`, sitemaps, `search/suggest.json`), code, docs, PRs.
- **Not allowed:** `shopify_publisher.py` (publish/update), `repair_schema.py`, `fix_untitled.py --apply`,
  `find_dupes.py --apply`, `collection_seo.py`/`push_collection.py`, landing publishers, theme or store-setting
  edits, any Shopify MCP / GraphQL / REST write, paid APIs, image generation, `persona_picker.py`, creating
  accounts, committing secrets (`.env`, `~/.genseo/*`, tokens, credentials).
- Publishing, images and every gate that needs Mac-only state (roster path, Admin API caches, ima2 OAuth) stay on
  the Macs. Hand work over as a ticket in `daily-tickets.md` or a draft in `published_drafts/` (gitignored).

## Hard rules (AGENTS.md)
1. No publish without `python3 scripts/validate_article.py <draft>.md --draft` → `✓ PASS`. Never edit a gate
   script to make something pass.
2. Publish/update only through `scripts/shopify_publisher.py` (it attaches the JSON-LD). Never hand-write JSON-LD.
3. Bylines only from `roster.json`; never invent a person, reviewer or credential (Dr./MD/PhD/RD/CISSN).
4. Link only products/collections that are live (`https://wellnessnest.co/products/<handle>.js`).
5. Refresh is append-only and never retitles a ranking page. Unattended runs never modify a live post.
6. Bulk writes: `backup_before_changes.py` → `--dry-run` → read → `--apply`. Never 301 a URL that still returns 200.
Also: never `rm` repo files (move them to `_superseded/`); never put CDN URLs in drafts.

